# What the image needs is the source tree. Nothing below is part of it: each
# path is either supplied at runtime by docker-compose.yml's mounts, or
# generated — by a build, by an e2e run, or by a tool nothing in the image
# calls.
#
# For the ones an e2e run rewrites, keeping them out matters beyond context
# size. A run regenerates the build output and the files it installs into the
# vault, so any of those reaching the context would invalidate `COPY . .` and
# store a fresh copy of the source tree on the next invocation, however
# little of it actually changed. With them excluded, a re-run that touched no
# source rebuilds nothing at all.
.git
node_modules
dist
.obsidian-cache

# Build output, assembled by esbuild.config.mjs and scripts/styles.mjs.
/main.js
/styles.css

# Installed into the vault by vault:install, and Obsidian's own UI state.
/test-vault/.obsidian/plugins/true-outliner/main.js
/test-vault/.obsidian/plugins/true-outliner/styles.css
/test-vault/.obsidian/plugins/true-outliner/manifest.json
/test-vault/.obsidian/workspace.json
/test-vault/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# Generated fixtures and reports: scripts/gen-backlink-hub.mjs, npm run
# test:coverage, and the design canvases.
/test-vault/Backlinks/Hub
/coverage
/design
